TEMPLATE — enriched-event fixture (EnrichedEvent skeleton).
DELETE EVERYTHING DOWN TO THE "---8<---" LINE; JSON HAS NO COMMENTS.

Modelled on old-orchestration/dags/sample_MEG_STARTED_context_enriched_event.json.
An enriched event is the raw EDF event merged with its resolved context — both
halves matter: Tier-1 and the control DAG match on "event", your calculator reads
run params from "context.data".

Substitute:
  {{source}}                   the publishing system, e.g. MERIVAL / MEGDP / AQUA_RISK_PLATFORM
                               — must match the IDENT in a SOURCE.* registry condition
  {{event_name}}               the EDF event name, e.g. D_MGDP_GLOBAL_TECH_START
  {{business_date}}            ISO date, e.g. 2026-07-26
  {{additional_data_fields}}   the fields the registered condition inspects (below)
  {{context_data_fields}}      the run params CALC_INIT will read

The condition type decides which "event.additionalData" fields MUST be present —
the validator warns when they are missing (registry-rules.md, trigger_conditions.py):

  SOURCE.*      "event.source"                     (already in the skeleton)
  CALC.*        "type": "CALC_EVENT", "STATE": "FINISH"
  DATASET.*     "DATASET_NAME": "...", "TYPE": "INGESTION"    (MERIVAL), or
                "megdpEventType": "data-update", "updateType": "CURATION"  (MEGDP)
  PIPELINEID.*  the pipeline identifier field

Typical context.data run params: company-code-1, runType, frequency, calcType,
h3Region, region, reporting-date, environment-name, enabledComponents, dag_id.
Use REAL values from the interview — never invent company codes or component lists.
